 "notes": [
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Use less than you think at first; more can always go in.</li><li>Taste once the coconut milk is in and correct the spices before adding the chickpeas.</li><li>If you want numbers to start from:<ul class=\"ing two-col\"><li><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"1\" data-s=\"0\">1 tsp</span> turmeric</li><li><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"1\" data-s=\"0\">1 tsp</span> chili powder</li><li><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"1\" data-b=\"2\" data-s=\"0\">1–2 tsp</span> cumin seeds</li><li>1 inch (~<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"cm\" data-a=\"2.5\" data-s=\"0\">2.5 cm</span>) fresh ginger</li><li>4–5 cloves garlic</li></ul></li><li>No two pots come out quite the same, and that’s fine.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Spicing by feel"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>More protein:<ul class=\"ing\"><li>paneer cubes (vegetarian)</li><li>tofu cubes (vegan)</li><li>hard-boiled eggs, added at the end</li></ul></li><li>In place of sweet potato:<ul class=\"ing\"><li>potato</li><li>cauliflower</li><li>butternut squash</li></ul></li><li>In place of spinach:<ul class=\"ing\"><li>kale</li><li>chard</li><li>mustard greens</li></ul></li><li>Richer:<ul class=\"ing\"><li>a spoonful of cashew butter</li><li>a knob of butter to finish (if not vegan)</li><li>half coconut cream, half coconut milk</li></ul></li><li>As a dal: swap in red lentils (20–25 min); it comes out looser, almost a soup — finish with lemon juice.</li><li>Other spices:<ul class=\"ing\"><li><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"1\" data-s=\"0\">1 tsp</span> garam masala at the end</li><li>curry leaves in with the cumin seeds</li><li>kasuri methi (dried fenugreek leaves)</li></ul></li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Swaps and extras"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Keeps 4–5 days in a sealed box in the fridge, or 3 months frozen.</li><li>Warm it on the stove with a little water.</li><li>It’s often better on day two.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "Storage"
  },
  {
   "html": "<p>Basmati rice, naan or roti, papadum, cucumber raita, mango chutney, lime pickle.</p>",
   "title_html": "Good with"
  },
  {
   "html": "<p>From Shivam’s recipe on <a href=\"https://prdp.net/recipe-folder/shivams-coconut-chickpeas\">prdp.net</a>, rewritten here.</p>",
   "title_html": "Credit"
  }
 ],
